    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d210">

                <pb facs="0242" n="238" sameAs="frus:frus1939v03/pg238"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.0146/722: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Japan</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Doomon</hi>)<anchor n="8a" xml:id="d210-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-09-07T19:00:00-04:00">September 7,
                            1939—7 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>277. Your 463, September 7, 6 p.m.<anchor n="9" xml:id="d210-f2"/> Following a
                    conference which I had at the White House, I requested the Japanese Ambassador
                    to call today at 5 p.m., at which time I made to him an oral statement
                    substantially as follows:</p>
                <p>[See memorandum of September 7 printed in <ref target="frus:frus1931-41v02/pg_12">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, Japan, 1931–1941, volume II,
                        page 12</ref>.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d210-f1" n="8a" type="source" xml:id="d210-f1-content">
                <p>The same telegram, with an introductory sentence, sent on the same date to the
                    Ambassadors in France and the United Kingdom as Nos. 818 and 844,
                    respectively.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d210-f2" n="9" xml:id="d210-f2-content">
                <p>
                    <ref target="frus1931-41v02#pg_15">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, Japan, 1931–1941, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">ii</hi>, p. 15</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
